{"id":"c287619d-3125-477d-8054-aac82940cc28","expr":"clazz.getModifiers() >= 0","rationale":"Modifiers are non-negative integers","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isStaticClass(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T00:43:20.250691104Z"}
{"id":"4b036476-9a00-4e92-8cd2-b1294ad36d6a","expr":"result == null || result.isAssignableFrom(clazz1)","rationale":"The result is either null or a common ancestor; thus result must be assignable from clazz1 if not null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T00:43:20.301785620Z"}
{"id":"5c3bb01a-f126-40b8-8391-918dadcff92c","expr":"result == null || result.isAssignableFrom(clazz2)","rationale":"Since the returned result is the common ancestor, it must be assignable from clazz2 when not null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T00:43:20.301785620Z"}
{"id":"261245e8-b8bd-4084-879f-4c6e90307c09","expr":"(clazz1 == null) == (result == clazz2)","rationale":"Method contract states if clazz1 is null then return is clazz2 and vice versa.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T00:43:20.301785620Z"}
{"id":"0736f2ec-c5a8-4f4f-b553-adf911fb2675","expr":"(clazz2 == null) == (result == clazz1)","rationale":"Method contract states if clazz2 is null then return is clazz1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T00:43:20.301785620Z"}
{"id":"3831a413-38ff-45b2-be18-1a1ac47a3c6a","expr":"(clazz1 != null && clazz2 != null) && (result == clazz1 || result == clazz2 || (result != null && result.isAssignableFrom(clazz1) && result.isAssignableFrom(clazz2)))","rationale":"At return, if both inputs are non-null, result is either clazz1, clazz2, or a common ancestor assignable from both.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#determineCommonAncestor(Class<?>,Class<?>):Class<?>","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T00:43:20.301785620Z"}
{"id":"065fc3d8-fefd-4b9b-9a1a-03ff5c0328d1","expr":"ifc != null && ifc.isInterface() == true","rationale":"ClassUtils.isJavaLanguageInterface likely checks for interface types, so ifc is expected to be an interface.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#isJavaLanguageInterface(Class<?>):boolean","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T00:43:20.675307227Z"}
