{"id":"2e8812aa-dec7-4b05-8939-ddaf22699d8c","expr":"clazz.isInterface() == false","rationale":"Typically, getStaticMethod will be used on concrete classes, but Class<?> can represent interfaces too. This is a useful but not strictly guaranteed condition.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getStaticMethod(Class<?>,String,Class<?>):Method","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T00:44:00.717984531Z"}
{"id":"736dcf80-9713-41db-987c-6239b96296c5","expr":"methodName.length() > 0","rationale":"Method name must not be null and normally a valid method name will have length greater than zero.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.util.ClassUtils#getStaticMethod(Class<?>,String,Class<?>):Method","file":"org/springframework/util/ClassUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T00:44:00.717984531Z"}
