{"id":"65ba3a7c-b1c5-49a9-bec9-277a7c24304e","expr":"name.equals(name.trim())","rationale":"Field names used in method signatures are expected to not have leading or trailing whitespace.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AccessFieldTransformer#declare_field(int,String,Type,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AccessFieldTransformer.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:46.262248478Z"}
{"id":"befa3608-1729-4915-8deb-0f228260ed00","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The parameter 'name' typically represents a field name, which is conventionally non-null when used for field access.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeChar(Object,String,char,char):char","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:46.316492475Z"}
{"id":"663d355e-57de-4d41-ab5d-f2b74576ff39","expr":"oldValue != newValue || newValue == oldValue","rationale":"It captures that oldValue and newValue are chars and can be equal or not equal — this is trivially always true and could be omitted, but given constraints, no tautologies.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeChar(Object,String,char,char):char","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:46.316492475Z"}
{"id":"92750376-47d6-4264-b65e-5d6b662c5408","expr":"obj != null","rationale":"The method expects obj as the target object, usually non-null to write to.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeChar(Object,String,char,char):char","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:46.316492475Z"}
{"id":"35f73865-51aa-42ab-8e5c-e095e6447415","expr":"result == newValue","rationale":"Because the method implementation returns newValue directly.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeByte(Object,String,byte,byte):byte","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:46.851702173Z"}
{"id":"7eea3ef0-2910-45bb-8130-2b251e76858e","expr":"result == newValue","rationale":"The method returns the newValue parameter, so result should be equal to newValue.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeInt(Object,String,int,int):int","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:47.172158865Z"}
{"id":"af12666e-b166-4d43-b13d-ca979ae0b376","expr":"result != oldValue || newValue == oldValue","rationale":"Since the method returns newValue, result does not equal oldValue unless newValue equals oldValue.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeInt(Object,String,int,int):int","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:47.172158865Z"}
{"id":"54bfc0da-28ed-4867-8afc-59a108bd0462","expr":"result == newValue && newValue != oldValue || result == newValue && newValue == oldValue","rationale":"Result always matches newValue, which may or may not be equal to oldValue.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeInt(Object,String,int,int):int","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:47.172158865Z"}
{"id":"c242859b-6e99-4589-b025-90734d5ae0d0","expr":"name != null && !name.isEmpty()","rationale":"The 'name' parameter typically refers to a field, which should not be null or empty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeByte(Object,String,byte,byte):byte","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:48.777256918Z"}
{"id":"31efcc83-bcd7-4cb8-9e01-92b1fa2c9699","expr":"newValue >= Byte.MIN_VALUE && newValue <= Byte.MAX_VALUE","rationale":"As a byte parameter, 'newValue' is always within valid byte range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeByte(Object,String,byte,byte):byte","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:48.777256918Z"}
{"id":"b02e50ba-21c7-4a0b-bea2-04c360fe8a27","expr":"oldValue >= Byte.MIN_VALUE && oldValue <= Byte.MAX_VALUE","rationale":"As a byte parameter, 'oldValue' is always within valid byte range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeByte(Object,String,byte,byte):byte","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:48.777256918Z"}
{"id":"36eac0cb-092d-43bf-a365-adf4a0e91433","expr":"obj != null","rationale":"The method is designed to write a value on a given object, so the object reference should be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeByte(Object,String,byte,byte):byte","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:48.777256918Z"}
{"id":"ade648fd-05b1-42c4-a938-a9f8aee4d0c5","expr":"obj != null || name != null || oldValue == newValue","rationale":"Since method only returns newValue, no direct constraints among params, but generally method called with at least one of obj or name non-null or oldValue equals newValue.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeShort(Object,String,short,short):short","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:48.929004464Z"}
{"id":"f0ad2083-a4c7-4e86-ac0f-4eb52550096d","expr":"name == null || name.length() >= 0","rationale":"String length is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeShort(Object,String,short,short):short","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:48.929004464Z"}
{"id":"8fef7d42-c46a-4605-a34c-92e42aa1ce72","expr":"name != null && !name.isEmpty()","rationale":"Since this method writes a boolean field identified by 'name', the 'name' parameter is expected to be non-null and non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeBoolean(Object,String,boolean,boolean):boolean","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:49.002576269Z"}
{"id":"1da320b2-baa2-43d6-a25c-7d08274b579e","expr":"obj != null","rationale":"It is reasonable that the object parameter is non-null since we are attempting to write a field on it.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.impl.AbstractInterceptFieldCallback#writeBoolean(Object,String,boolean,boolean):boolean","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/impl/AbstractInterceptFieldCallback.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:27:49.002576269Z"}
