{"id":"a2a69584-6656-4c03-9929-b9d2db9a878f","expr":"type >= 0 && type <= 8","rationale":"Type must be one of the predefined Opcodes frame types (e.g., F_NEW, F_FULL, etc.), generally between 0 and 8 inclusive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:38:54.816602557Z"}
{"id":"186af23b-9ee8-4c33-8515-c2efdb5a748a","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode < 256","rationale":"opcode is a valid bytecode instruction value index","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:38:56.744367353Z"}
{"id":"8c9539c7-9c62-4025-ba51-c10b5e32502b","expr":"opcode == (opcode & 0xFF)","rationale":"opcode fits in a byte","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:38:56.744367353Z"}
{"id":"fc4f0a0d-2726-4d21-b8bb-7791de334ef3","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indices are generally non-negative in bytecode manipulation.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:01.587449027Z"}
{"id":"74ecf04b-722e-4608-8a0a-fe537fbdd2be","expr":"varIndex < 256 || varIndex >= 256","rationale":"Bytecode instructions differentiate between varIndex < 256 and varIndex >= 256 cases.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:01.587449027Z"}
{"id":"26ebccc4-1d71-4b12-be9c-5cd7a248ffc8","expr":"(varIndex < 4 || varIndex >= 4)","rationale":"The optimization for opcode depends on varIndex being less than 4 or not.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:01.587449027Z"}
{"id":"81b1e301-e305-48e0-85e7-d9d55646c1a8","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indices in JVM bytecode are always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:08.209753091Z"}
{"id":"6215545e-ba65-4f5f-ab71-759702493363","expr":"type != null && !type.isEmpty()","rationale":"The parameter 'type' typically refers to a class descriptor, which should be a valid non-empty string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:12.303521023Z"}
{"id":"1ec66ccd-af9e-4c63-a728-62b6a6192ffe","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"The 'opcode' parameter is expected to be a valid bytecode instruction code within byte range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:12.303521023Z"}
{"id":"cf27d456-57de-472a-a620-313db9d704b2","expr":"type.equals(type.trim())","rationale":"Ensures the 'type' string does not contain extraneous whitespace around it.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:12.303521023Z"}
{"id":"e9b37b88-5c9a-4c3e-9949-2a69957694dc","expr":"owner != null && !owner.isEmpty()","rationale":"The owner string commonly represents an internal JVM class name, so it should be non-null and non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:19.012661864Z"}
{"id":"74db74c2-2cb2-41b2-b07d-2c39dab84976","expr":"name != null && !name.isEmpty()","rationale":"Field name should be a valid non-empty string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:19.012661864Z"}
{"id":"4bb1ead4-7194-45c2-bdfd-41ce5d26cd96","expr":"descriptor != null && !descriptor.isEmpty()","rationale":"Descriptor string represents the field type and should not be empty.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:19.012661864Z"}
{"id":"577b9af6-0286-4421-a5f3-39ccbb5dc790","expr":"opcode >= 178 && opcode <= 181","rationale":"The opcodes for field instructions are GETSTATIC (178), PUTSTATIC (179), GETFIELD (180), PUTFIELD (181).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:19.012661864Z"}
{"id":"dac40b00-43c1-47fc-8c87-e006c2a0e509","expr":"owner != null && !owner.isEmpty()","rationale":"The owner string should be a valid internal class name representation and thus non-null and non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:28.506449138Z"}
{"id":"e56e32e6-d561-4b63-84b7-eef62895bfb9","expr":"name != null && !name.isEmpty()","rationale":"Field names are expected to be valid, non-empty identifiers.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:28.506449138Z"}
{"id":"72985719-6172-4761-b98f-1880adfd264a","expr":"descriptor != null && !descriptor.isEmpty()","rationale":"Field descriptors are a required type descriptor string so must be non-null and non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:28.506449138Z"}
{"id":"9a38c40f-dc56-4e3f-87c0-bb824d75b372","expr":"owner != null && name != null && descriptor != null && (opcode == 0 || opcode == 1 || opcode == 2 || opcode == 3)","rationale":"The opcode parameter should be one of the valid invoke instruction opcodes, typically constants such as INVOKEVIRTUAL, INVOKESPECIAL, INVOKESTATIC, or INVOKEINTERFACE, represented by integers. owner, name, and descriptor are strings identifying the method and are typically non-null when visiting a method instruction.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:32.393487108Z"}
{"id":"b0394285-f838-43eb-b51e-234c3251bea1","expr":"name.length() > 0","rationale":"The name of the method being invoked should be a non-empty string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:32.393487108Z"}
{"id":"6668d85a-a45d-43ca-8673-fcba6f06fac9","expr":"descriptor.startsWith(\"(\") && descriptor.contains(\")\")","rationale":"Descriptors follow the JVM method descriptor syntax, starting with '(' and containing ')' separating argument types and return type.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:39:32.393487108Z"}
{"id":"953cd61c-58cf-4dde-8eed-add4290f24d2","expr":"name != null && !name.isEmpty()","rationale":"The name parameter is typically non-null and non-empty for method invocation names.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:41:10.740306945Z"}
{"id":"7ac57552-9cb9-4c20-ad88-3c9dd5e04ac5","expr":"descriptor != null && descriptor.startsWith(\"(\") && descriptor.contains(\")\")","rationale":"Method descriptors for invokedynamic instructions follow JVM descriptor syntax.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:41:10.740306945Z"}
{"id":"3d6de3c9-3e67-4ec7-b869-20e11f9725c6","expr":"bootstrapMethodHandle != null","rationale":"The bootstrap method handle is required to identify the bootstrap method for invokedynamic.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-11T01:41:10.740306945Z"}
